# Drafted by Gemini (R14 hook), edited.

~ weston_pilgrim
weston_murdoch [weary]: Friends, two of our flock, Melina and Gareth Creed, walked west to hear the great bell at Silverbell Monastery. They found Dawn's Gate changed and dark.
weston_murdoch [sad]: A stable hand pulled Gareth aside to whisper some secret, and neither boy nor hand came back. Only Melina made it home.
* What does Gareth look like? -> weston_gareth
* Where can we find Melina? -> weston_melina
* Tell us about the road west. -> weston_road
* We will find him. -> weston_go
* Not yet. -> weston_later

~ weston_gareth
weston_murdoch [smile]: Tall, dark hair, a neat short beard, and grey eyes that do not blink at trouble. Good heart, though he is stubborn as an oak fencepost.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A clean description and a three-day trail. We shall have his spoor before sundown, friends.
-> weston_pilgrim

~ weston_melina
weston_murdoch [neutral]: She sits near the church steps, jumped at every shadow since she stumbled back. Speak gently with her before you set out.
-> weston_pilgrim

~ weston_road
weston_murdoch [weary]: Cross the Silverbell by bridge or ferry, then follow the south bank three nights, about fourteen hours' march. Folks say the village at the end is dead afraid.
-> weston_pilgrim

~ weston_go
set gareth_asked
quest crimson_monastery heard
weston_murdoch [smile]: May the songbird's wing keep you in the dark, friends. Bring our loud brother back to the choir if the road allows.
Narrator: The preacher's hand is warm with candle-tallow and honest worry, and the western wind smells faintly of river mud and distant snow.
-> END

~ weston_later
weston_murdoch [neutral]: Keep our lost bird in your prayers until your boots are ready, friends.
-> END

~ melina_wait
set melina_met
melina [afraid]: Have you word from the river road? No, pardon me, you have not even left yet, my wits are all scattered.
* Tell us about Gareth. -> melina_gareth
* What did you see in Dawn's Gate? -> melina_saw
* [if not flag.melina_token] Ask for something Gareth would know -> melina_token
* Leave her for now. -> END

~ melina_gareth
melina [sad]: He is mule-headed when he thinks a soul needs help, and he sings louder than anyone in the choir, never once on the right note.
melina [afraid]: Tell him Melina sent you, and he will stop arguing long enough to listen.
-> melina_wait

~ melina_saw
melina [afraid]: When the mountain bells rang, the whole town dropped to their knees in the dirt. A boy by the stables whispered something that turned Gareth pale.
interject name:silas_vane: Whole village folding on a single bell-ring. Somebody up that crag holds a stacked deck.
melina [sad]: Above us, those great monastery windows burned red as open sores against the snow. Gareth told me to run, and Heaven forgive me, I ran.
-> melina_wait

~ melina_token
melina [sad]: Here, take this little lark I whittled from ash wood. He carries its twin in his coat pocket, so he will know you come from me.
give melinas_songbird
set melina_token
-> melina_wait

~ weston_return
set mon_returned
quest crimson_monastery done
set phillip_dinner_invited
gold +100
if flag.gareth_fate == "rescued"
weston_murdoch [smile]: You brought him back whole! Melina has not stopped weeping for joy, and Gareth is already singing off-key at the top of his lungs.
Narrator: Through the church doors drifts a bright, ragged chorus, one booming baritone cheerfully dragging half a beat behind the rest.
else
weston_murdoch [sad]: We held Gareth's service by the old stones tonight. He stayed behind for a stranger's sake, and I mean to put his name forward for sainthood.
Narrator: Candle smoke hangs blue and sweet beneath the rafters, where the choir hums a low hymn without its loudest voice.
endif
if flag.crimson_faith_disbanded
weston_murdoch [weary]: Stragglers from that mountain cult are already wandering into Wickermoor, blinking like moles, and our three faiths are squabbling over who gets to save them first.
endif
weston_murdoch [neutral]: Before I forget, a footman left a heavy cream card for you. Lord Phillip Druskenvald invites you all to supper at the Druskenvald Estate.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Heavy cream stationery and an estate supper? Do let me calibrate my vials before we dine.
-> END

~ melina_reunion
if flag.gareth_fate == "rescued"
melina [smile]: Look here, both little wooden birds back in one nest. Thank you for bringing my stubborn fool home to me.
else
melina [sad]: You walked into that red dark for him, and you brought me the truth of his end. I am grateful you tried, truly I am.
endif
melina [weary]: Go on in out of the wind when you can, friends.
-> END
